            category: "Red raspberries, summer-bearing",
            harvest_time_unparsed: "early",
            description:
                "From New York. Early. Hardy, tall, vigorous, productive canes. Good-quality fruit. May bear a small fall primocane crop in southern Maine"
        },
        {
            type: "Raspberry",
            name: "Reveille",
            category: "Red raspberries, summer-bearing",
            harvest_time_unparsed: "early",
            description:
                "From Maryland. Early. Very hardy, vigorous, suckering, high-yielding plants. Medium to large fruit with good flavor, very soft, poor for shipping and freezing"
        },
        {
            type: "Raspberry",
            name: "Boyne",
            category: "Red raspberries, summer-bearing",
            harvest_time_unparsed: "early",
            description:
                "From Manitoba. Early with excellent winter hardiness. Spiny, suckering plants. Small to medium dark soft fruit, fair flavor, good freezing quality. Susceptible to anthracnose. Recommended for colder sites"
        },
        {
            type: "Raspberry",
            name: "Killarney",
            category: "Red raspberries, summer-bearing",
            harvest_time_unparsed: "early",
            description:
                "From Manitoba. Early, slightly after Boyne. Hardy, spiny, suckering plants. Medium bright red fruit with good flavor and freezing quality. Susceptible to mildew and anthracnose. Recommended for colder sites"
        },
        {
            type: "Raspberry",
            name: "Canby",
            category: "Red raspberries, summer-bearing",
            harvest_time_unparsed: "mid-season",
            description:
                "From Oregon. Mid-season with moderate hardiness. Tall nearly thornless plants. Medium to large firm bright red fruit with excellent flavor. Buds may winter-kill in cold climates"
        },
        {
            type: "Raspberry",
            name: "Eden",
            category: "Red raspberries, summer-bearing",
            harvest_time_unparsed: "mid-season",
            description:
                "From Nova Scotia. Mid-season. Hardy spineless plants with tall vigorous canes. Large firm light red very sweet fruit. May lack hardiness in northern locations"
        },
        {
            type: "Raspberry",
            name: "Latham",
            category: "Red raspberries, summer-bearing",
            harvest_time_unparsed: "mid-season",
            description:
                "From Minnesota. Mid-season and very hardy. Vigorous plants with few spines. Small fruit with good color, fair flavor, crumbly texture, and a long ripening period. Recommended for colder sites"
        },
        {
            type: "Raspberry",
            name: "Newburgh",
            category: "Red raspberries, summer-bearing",
            harvest_time_unparsed: "mid-season",
            description:
                "From New York. Mid-season and hardy. Tall, moderately vigorous plants with few spines. Partly resistant to common cane diseases and root rot. Medium light red fruit with good flavor, sometimes crumbly and uneven ripening"
        },
        {
            type: "Raspberry",
            name: "Nova",
            category: "Red raspberries, summer-bearing",
            harvest_time_unparsed: "mid-season",
            description:
                "From Nova Scotia. Very hardy with good vigor and few thorns. Appears resistant to most common cane diseases. Mid-season, attractive, medium, firm, bright red, somewhat acidic fruit"
        },
        {
            type: "Raspberry",
            name: "Taylor",
            category: "Red raspberries, summer-bearing",
            harvest_time_unparsed: "late",
            description:
                "From New York. Late and moderately hardy. Vigorous tall canes with some spines. Very susceptible to mosaic virus, leaf spot, and fungal diseases. Medium to large fruit with excellent flavor, color, and firmness"
        },
        {
            type: "Raspberry",
            name: "Encore",
            category: "Red raspberries, summer-bearing",
            harvest_time_unparsed: "late",
            description:
                "From New York. Late. Hardy, productive, vigorous plants with tall canes and large good-quality fruit"
        },
        {
            type: "Raspberry",
            name: "Polana",
            category: "Red raspberries, everbearing",
            harvest_time_unparsed: "very early fall crop",
            description:
                "Very early fall crop. Vigorous, short, productive canes. Small to medium attractive fruit, many misshapen and difficult to pick, fair flavor. Recommended for northern short-season areas"
        },
        {
            type: "Raspberry",
            name: "Polka",
            category: "Red raspberries, everbearing",
            harvest_time_unparsed: "early fall crop",
            description:
